eration Army. Sabara Megumi was born in the Kyushu region of Japan in 1933 and came to Northeast China with his parents when he was a child. After Japan's defeat and surrender, he was unable to return to Japan, and lived at a landlord’s house in Liaoning to herd cattle. In 1948, he joined the People’s Liberation Army under the name of “Zhang Rongqing”, where he experienced the battles of Liaoshen and Pingjin and devoted himself to the cause of the proletarian revolution.\n\n(Source: Bilibili, translated)"},"tags":[{"name":"Historical","rank":80,"spoiler":false},{"name":"Class Struggle","rank":79,"spoiler":false},{"name":"Biographical","rank":73,"spoiler":false},{"name":"Military","rank":50,"spoiler":false},{"name":"War","rank":50,"spoiler":false},{"name":"Male Protagonist","rank":50,"spoiler":false},{"name":"Foreign","rank":20,"spoiler":false},{"name":"Mixed Media","rank":20,"spoiler":false}],"titles":{"display":"Blood and heart: The legendary life of a Japanese youth in China","english":"Blood and heart: The legendary life of a Japanese youth in China","native":"血与心","romaji":"Xue Yu Xin","synonyms":[]},"trailer":{"id":"msje2ACg3-8","site":"youtube","thumbnail":"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/msje2ACg3-8/hqdefault.jpg"},"visibility":"general"}